948
01:16:18.280 --> 01:16:22.960
However, know that I too suffered this pain.

949
01:16:22.960 --> 01:16:30.160
When they crucified me, they stretched me on the cross so much as to tear all my nerves.

950
01:16:30.160 --> 01:16:32.920
Now I presume he's not exaggerating.

951
01:16:32.920 --> 01:16:36.360
All my nerves is beyond belief, isn't it?

952
01:16:36.360 --> 01:16:42.240
To the point that I felt them snap and twist.

953
01:16:42.240 --> 01:16:48.920
And those of my throat suffered a greater pain and tearing, which was such that I felt

954
01:16:48.920 --> 01:16:49.920
suffocated.

955
01:16:49.920 --> 01:16:55.640
Hence his loud cry, his last cry from the cross, had to come from his divinity through his

956
01:16:55.640 --> 01:16:59.880
humanity because his humanity couldn't do it.

957
01:16:59.880 --> 01:17:07.560
It was the cry of humanity submerged by passions which clasping my throat drowned me with its

958
01:17:07.560 --> 01:17:10.320
pains.

959
01:17:10.320 --> 01:17:14.400
This pain of mine was terrible and horrible.

960
01:17:14.400 --> 01:17:19.360
How I felt the nerves and the bones of my throat being stretched to the point of feeling

961
01:17:19.360 --> 01:17:26.800
all the nerves of my head, of my mouth, and even of my eyes being snapped.

962
01:17:26.800 --> 01:17:32.560
It's horrendous even to read it, isn't it?

963
01:17:32.560 --> 01:17:40.160
The tension was such that every small movement made me feel mortal pains.

964
01:17:40.160 --> 01:17:45.840
I would become motionless, and then I would ride so much as to batter against the cross

965
01:17:45.840 --> 01:17:47.360
